# C++ Programming Course

## Class and Object (OOP)
- Theory, Pillars (`Encapsulation`, `Polymorphism`, `Inheritance`, `Abstraction`) and Applications
- Encapsulation and `class object` concept
- `public` and `private` access modifier and initialize fields - `Student.cpp`
- Taking user input and initialzie fields - `Employee.cpp`
- Setter/Mutator concept - `Circle.cpp`
- Getter/Accessor concept - `Rectangle.cpp`
- `this` keyword using `Triangle.cpp` when conflicts identifier (There are many use cases though) 
- `private` access modifier and data hiding concept using `BankAccount.cpp`
- `constructor or object builder` theory and types
- `non parameterized constructor` concept using `Trapezium.cpp`
- `parameterized constructor` concept using `Car.cpp`
- `copy constructor` concept using `Sphere.cpp`
- `object orientation` - `Library.cpp`
- `destructor or object destroyer` and concept of `stack and heap` memory - `Destructor.cpp`
- Destruct the heap array using `delete[]` - `DestructorArrayHeap.cpp`

## Method Overloading / Compile Time Polymorphism / Static Binding
- Basic Idea using `Printer.java` of exact parameter type matching
- Type auto promotion idea using `Finder.java` when exact match failed
- Ambiguity problem when multiple match `Matcher.java`

## Inheritance
- Inheritance Theory (Definitin, Types, Advantages and Idea)
- Single Inheritance: `extends` keyword and Constructor Chaining using `Parent.java` and `super()` 
- Single Inheritance: Accessing methods `Person.java` 
- Hierarchical Inheritance: Implementation using `Vehicle.java`
- Multilevel Inheritance: Implementation using `Grandfather.java`
- Multiple Inheritance: Implementation using `CEO.java` - `(Diamond Problem)`
- Hybrid Inheritance: Implementation using `Hybrid.java`

## Method Overriding / Runtime Polymorphism / Dynamic Binding
- Basic Overriding using `Shape.java`   
- Real life example using `Employee.java` and super class method calling by `super keyword`
- Common Confusion about Upcasting using `Animal.java`
- Complexity of Downcasting using `Man.java`

## java.lang.Object Class (Topmost Class of Java)
- `User Comparison` using `toString()` method of `java.lang.Object` class (Our class is `User.java`)


## Access Modifiers (default, public, private, protected)
- Compiler Generated Constructor
```JAVA
public ConstructorName() {
    super();
}
```
|Modifier Name| Same Class | Same Package | Subclass (Other Package) | Other Classes | 
|------|--------|-----|------|-------|
| default | ✔️  |  ✔️ | ❌ | ❌  |
| private | ✔️  |  ️❌ |  ❌ | ❌  |
| public  | ️ ✔️ |  ✔️️ | ✔️  |  ✔️️ |
| protected |✔️ |  ✔️ | ✔️ |  ❌️ |